**How to implement.** An experiment's attachment is checked when its experiments are opened (001 §E 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open'; the S4.2 brief: the status function runs on open). Today the constructor opens experiments by loading a saved collection (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, the `CollectionLoad` arm of `updateTableAndElementRotation`), and that arm clears every status. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `ExperimentFileStatus` (step 135) gains `DataFileChangedSinceAttach`, captioned `Data changed since attach — attach it again to validate it`, and `DataFileMissingFromKit of path : ControlCaption`, captioned `Data file missing — <path>`, each with a one-line doc. (2) The `CollectionLoad` arm, on `Ok (Some snapshot)`, sets `experimentDataStatus` to one status for each loaded experiment that has an attachment, through `model.experimentData.attachmentStatus` (step 135). `AttachedDataUnchanged` validates it as attaching does (`loadAndValidate`, giving `DataFileValidated` or the error's status). `AttachedDataChanged _` is `DataFileChangedSinceAttach`. `AttachedDataMissing` is `DataFileMissingFromKit` of the kit path. An `Error e` is `AttachedFileParseError e.caption`, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:fileStatus` maps a read failure today. An experiment without an attachment has no status. The validation of the attach arm and of this arm is one private function, so it is written once. Its comment cites 001 §E in one line, where the clear-on-load comment stood. No other arm, field or message changes. Tests, in `InverseConstructorTests`. `loading a collection re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged`: a collection saved with an attachment and loaded into a fresh model sharing the collection store, over a mock whose `attachmentStatus` answers `AttachedDataUnchanged`, gives that experiment the status `DataFileValidated` with the mock's point count. `loading a collection flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`: a collection of two experiments, attached at `data/a.csv` and `data/b.csv`, loaded over a mock whose `attachmentStatus` answers `AttachedDataChanged` for the first and `AttachedDataMissing` for the second, gives them the statuses `DataFileChangedSinceAttach` and `DataFileMissingFromKit`, whose caption names `data/b.csv`, and the loaded experiments keep their attachments.

**Acceptance.** After a collection loads, every loaded experiment with an attachment MUST carry a status computed through `attachmentStatus`: validated when unchanged, `DataFileChangedSinceAttach` when its data changed and `DataFileMissingFromKit` when it is gone; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `loading a collection re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged` and `loading a collection flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.
